<title>USA: Arterial doesn't see FDA ok before 1998.</title>
<headline>Arterial doesn't see FDA ok before 1998.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA ROSA, Calif 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arterial Vascular Engineering Inc said early Monday that it does not expect Food and Drug Administration approval of its stent products for sale in the United States before 1998.</p>
<p>The company said additionally in a release that &quot;there can be no assurance when or if approval will be obtained.&quot;</p>
<p>Stents are medical devices inserted into arteries after ballon angioplasty to prevent blockages.</p>
<p>The company's shares closed Friday up 3/8 at 14-3/8.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
